From bfbbe5aa3898c7ad08f8134d6c6b89f13acda29c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "nipuna.dulara" <pererannd.21@uom.lk>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 13:06:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] nr: Aggregate gNB energy per carrier, not per bandwidth
 part

Reconcile the energy models with their attached EnergySource, then add
multi-carrier support: normalise sf to the carrier's bandwidth rather
than the reporting bandwidth part's, so a carrier split into several
BWPs is not charged several times over for the same baseline power, and
make sp a carrier property for the same reason. Add
NrGnbEnergyAggregator to sum a multi-carrier gNB's per-carrier power,
deriving the TR 38.864 Section 5.1 0.7 contiguous-CC weighting from
each carrier's real spectrum position instead of taking it as a
caller-supplied parameter. Key the energy model tables by name instead
of positional index, and extend the gNB listener test to cover its real
behaviour rather than just its defaults.
